WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.713
Every danger here is a
way evidence can lie.

2
00:00:02.713 --> 00:00:05.804
The quietest is a failed
read that looks like a fix:

3
00:00:05.804 --> 00:00:09.574
a permissions error, and
yesterday's findings simply vanish.

4
00:00:09.574 --> 00:00:13.450
The code marks the task as an error
and keeps those findings open.

5
00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:15.634
Close behind is a day nobody read,

6
00:00:15.634 --> 00:00:18.788
which would let a gate pass
on the days that were.

7
00:00:18.788 --> 00:00:22.745
Others are about trust: names
leaking into the tracker,

8
00:00:22.745 --> 00:00:26.438
a run edited or swapped, a
package quietly replaced.

9
00:00:26.438 --> 00:00:30.134
And one is about attention:
count every activation as drift,

10
00:00:30.134 --> 00:00:32.900
and people stop reading
the incident queue.
